Third-party material
--------------------

This project is a tool for QMK firmware and carries material derived from
it. QMK is GPL-2.0, which is why this project is too.

* QMK Firmware — https://github.com/qmk/qmk_firmware — GPL-2.0
  Copyright the QMK contributors.

  - `shared/moonlander_geometry.json` is extracted mechanically from
    `keyboards/zsa/moonlander/revb/keyboard.json` by
    `scripts/extract-geometry.mjs` (key positions, matrix addresses and the
    LED map).
  - `shared/keycodes.json` uses QMK keycode names and aliases.
  - The firmware this app generates targets QMK and uses its keymap,
    combo, tap-dance and `SEND_STRING` constructs. Behavioural claims in
    the code and in `docs/CONTRACT.md` cite QMK source locations, notably
    `quantum/keycode_config.c` (the Ctrl<->Cmd magic swap),
    `quantum/quantum.c` (`register_code16`) and `quantum/os_detection.c`.

* ZSA Moonlander / Oryx — https://www.zsa.io — ZSA Technology Labs
  The Moonlander keyboard definition in QMK is maintained by ZSA. Layouts
  are seeded from Oryx, ZSA's layout configurator, and the generated
  firmware reproduces the `zsa/oryx` community-module constructs
  (`DUAL_FUNC_n`, `ST_MACRO_n`, `HSV_h_s_v`) so that a layout authored in
  Oryx keeps behaving the same way once this app owns it.

  - `shared/fixtures/reference_keymap.c` and `reference_config.h` are Oryx
    output, kept as the golden reference the code generator is tested
    against.

Dependencies are declared in `package.json` and `src-tauri/Cargo.toml` and
are not vendored here; their licences are their own.
